  "scope": "Stage E, E3: the 13 legacy Profile HTTP routes answer 410. Prior tests migrate per the owner-approved E3 test map. A test whose subject is a retired route is removed (a file whose every test retired keeps only its docstring naming the successors). A test whose subject survives is adapted: setup through a retired route moves to the native route, a direct store seed, or the shared OAuth-flow seeder; observations through a retired route move to the Connection API, the provider-access listing or the stored document/Connection state. Assertions that checked only a retired route's own HTTP answer during setup (e.g. start.status_code == 201, the profile_id of the start answer) or its projection (the /status body) are removed or reduced to the stored state; no storage-state assertion is weakened. The two OpenAPI tests that pinned the legacy profile paths are flipped to pin their absence and renamed accordingly. D1: a race whose only legacy actor is a retired route retires; an intruder against a surviving subject moves to the native route or set_pair_api_key with assertions unchanged.",
  "reason": "OME-1209 spec R1 retires the Profile routes; their handlers and schemas are deleted, so tests driving them can no longer run. Owner decisions 2026-10-18 (D1-D4, the test map, and the assertion edits beyond the map that only checked retired HTTP answers).",
